Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:12:07 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 51/78] PlaitOS: adapt always-on display schedule to GrapheneOS

- Keys are Settings.Secure plait_doze_always_on_auto_mode (0 off, the
  default) and plait_doze_always_on_auto_time instead of new Settings API
  constants
- The schedule string is parsed defensively: this runs in system_server and
  a malformed value used to throw on every boot (bootloop); bad values now
  fall back to 20:00-07:00 with a log line
- Ignore settings changes until boot completed (twilight and the prefs file
  are not ready before; initState(true) runs then anyway) and null-check the
  remaining unguarded shared preferences uses
- Never wake the screen fully when the schedule turns AOD on with pulsing
  off (it lit the screen at the scheduled time, in a pocket too); refresh
  doze with the pulse broadcast only, and drop the now unused helpers

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNZzm3ssZ7eH5QDg4P9AiP
